// Canonical source: get and put on a field create its read and write methods
// (thesis lines 659-660), so a private field with get reads from outside and
// one with put takes a set from outside; the class's own code reads all three.
// Answer: 43 (4 + 30 + 9).
class P : Object { section [private] { int shown [get]; int both [get, put]; int secret; }
  section [public] { P() { this.shown = 4; this.both = 1; this.secret = 9; } int Secret() { return this.secret; } } }
P p = new P();
p.both = 30;
return p.shown + p.both + p.Secret();
